+A release is a promise about a file: that the name says which version it is and which machine it
+was built for, that the bytes are the ones that were tested, and that somebody reading the version
+number can find out what changed in it. Everything on this page is one of those three.
 
-## The commands
+A release of this project is the two binaries, [`jobqd`](../src/bin/jobqd.rs) and
+[`jobqc`](../src/bin/jobqc.rs), plus [`SHA256SUMS`](../src/engine/release.rs) — a checksum file in
+the format `sha256sum -c` reads. They are written into a directory named `jobq-<version>-<target>`,
+and the version in that name is the version in [`Cargo.toml`](../Cargo.toml) — there is one copy of
+it, and the tag is checked against it rather than typed a second time.
 
